[{"id":68985,"sender_id":639,"sender_full_name":"Praphulla Koushik","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/4d3ba0c0a767b7329e0f56993aceb259?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/1-nLab/topic/Images.20instead.20of.20codes.20rendering/near/68985\">#1</a> Hello,</p>\n<p>Is it a better idea to add images instead of writing latex code and rendering it here?\nDiagrams do not seem to be as good as in say some wordpress site.</p>\n<p>There are some restrictions on what codes one can render (I guess tikzcd is not possible to render). So, I think it is better to add images so that it looks better.</p>","timestamp":1531246075,"subject":"Images instead of codes rendering","stream_id":1,"display_recipient":"nLab","reactions":[]},{"id":68986,"sender_id":237,"sender_full_name":"Richard Williamson","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b90dbe6063b47a44f7308efebb6ade2b?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/1-nLab/topic/Images.20instead.20of.20codes.20rendering/near/68986\">#2</a> Good idea in my view! Just upload the pictures to the nLab, so they do not disappear. I have ideas of including tikz in my reworking of the rendering, but no idea when I will find the time.</p>","timestamp":1531249241,"subject":"Images instead of codes rendering","stream_id":1,"display_recipient":"nLab","reactions":[]},{"id":68989,"sender_id":10,"sender_full_name":"Mike Shulman","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ede34282f405f902e12fa7e6cf336572?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/1-nLab/topic/Images.20instead.20of.20codes.20rendering/near/68989\">#3</a> I would actually say no: please use the nLab math formatting facilities whenever possible.  The big problem with uploading pictures is that it is much more difficult for other people editing a page to modify them.  The fact that anyone can edit any part of a page is fundamental to the meaning of a wiki like the nLab; it’s regrettable that our diagrams don’t look quite as nice, but I don’t think a slightly improved appearance justifies breaking the basic nature of a wiki.  (When it comes to diagrams that literally <em>can’t</em> be reproduced in our wiki-syntax, then I think it’s more acceptable, but I generally just try to avoid such diagrams.)</p>\n<p>Diagrams should definitely go on the <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlabmeta/show/Technical%20TODO%20List\">Technical TODO List (nlabmeta)</a>!</p>","timestamp":1531259845,"subject":"Images instead of codes rendering","stream_id":1,"display_recipient":"nLab","reactions":[]},{"id":68990,"sender_id":78,"sender_full_name":"RodMcGuire","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/93dc0f9f03cdabb6b19a1522bd94c69f?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/1-nLab/topic/Images.20instead.20of.20codes.20rendering/near/68990\">#4</a></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>please use the nLab math formatting facilities whenever possible. The big problem with uploading pictures is that it is much more difficult for other people editing a page to modify them. </p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I agree, that is at least for images that have been generated rather that captured by a screen grab.</p>\n<p>The nLab could use some sort of subsystem for generated images that keeps around their source code and can regenerate them as PNGs or SVG. Wikipedia sort of has a convention of providing source for images but doesn’t address regeneration. See <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:5_lemma.svg\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:5_lemma.svg</a>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:2-commutative-diagram.pdf.svg\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:2-commutative-diagram.pdf.svg</a>, and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Categorical_pullback_(expanded).svg\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Categorical_pullback_(expanded).svg</a>.</p>","timestamp":1531263725,"subject":"Images instead of codes rendering","stream_id":1,"display_recipient":"nLab","reactions":[]},{"id":68991,"sender_id":10,"sender_full_name":"Mike Shulman","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ede34282f405f902e12fa7e6cf336572?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/1-nLab/topic/Images.20instead.20of.20codes.20rendering/near/68991\">#5</a> Instiki does include an SVG editor.  However, in practice it doesn’t seem to be very practical.  Maybe the ideal would be a syntax that one could type into the source of a page that would result in the server rendering a <code>standalone</code> latex document to get an image that it would save and then automatically include when displaying the page.</p>\n<p>Of course, another disadvantage with images of any sort is that they don’t scale the way text does when a page is zoomed.</p>","timestamp":1531264333,"subject":"Images instead of codes rendering","stream_id":1,"display_recipient":"nLab","reactions":[]},{"id":68992,"sender_id":78,"sender_full_name":"RodMcGuire","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/93dc0f9f03cdabb6b19a1522bd94c69f?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/1-nLab/topic/Images.20instead.20of.20codes.20rendering/near/68992\">#6</a></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Of course, another disadvantage with images of any sort is that they don’t scale the way text does when a page is zoomed.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>A <code>.svg</code> file is an image file that can be anywhere that say a <code>.png</code> file can, and they do scale. The Wikipedia examples I listed above indicate that there is a way to go from <code>tex</code> to <code>svg</code>.</p>\n<p>One does want SVG files not to contain characters but instead svg encodings of them to avoid the layout problems caused by different people having different default fonts.</p>","timestamp":1531267655,"subject":"Images instead of codes rendering","stream_id":1,"display_recipient":"nLab","reactions":[]},{"id":68994,"sender_id":639,"sender_full_name":"Praphulla Koushik","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/4d3ba0c0a767b7329e0f56993aceb259?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/1-nLab/topic/Images.20instead.20of.20codes.20rendering/near/68994\">#7</a> How about posting the diagram as well as code hidden just near the diagram?</p>\n<p>% something when you render in some latex compiler will hide that something.</p>\n<p>So, you can write the code in that % so that it is not visible unless you try to edit and any one who want to edit the diagram can use the code.</p>","timestamp":1531278049,"subject":"Images instead of codes rendering","stream_id":1,"display_recipient":"nLab","reactions":[]},{"id":68995,"sender_id":10,"sender_full_name":"Mike Shulman","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ede34282f405f902e12fa7e6cf336572?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/1-nLab/topic/Images.20instead.20of.20codes.20rendering/near/68995\">#8</a> Sorry, of course in <a href=\"#narrow/channel/1-nLab/topic/Images.20instead.20of.20codes.20rendering/near/68991\">#5</a> I meant to say “bitmap images”.  SVG is, as it says on the tin, the <em>Scalable</em> Vector Graphics format.  Converting LaTeX/TikZ to SVG seems like a good idea, although judging by the answers <a href=\"https://tex.stackexchange.com/questions/255470/compile-tex-directly-into-svg-using-the-command-line\">here</a> we might have to go through PDF or DVI first.</p>\n<p>I don’t think instiki currently has a way to insert “comments” in the source that aren’t rendered at all in the browser, does it?  If it did, I suppose including the source alongside the image would be one approach, but it would require every editor to manually compile, image-ify, and re-upload the diagram, which isn’t ideal.</p>","timestamp":1531281458,"subject":"Images instead of codes rendering","stream_id":1,"display_recipient":"nLab","reactions":[]},{"id":69000,"sender_id":237,"sender_full_name":"Richard Williamson","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b90dbe6063b47a44f7308efebb6ade2b?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/1-nLab/topic/Images.20instead.20of.20codes.20rendering/near/69000\">#9</a> Mike’s points are good ones. Maybe you could use standard nLab code for simple diagrams, Praphulla, and images for the others. You should be able to use HTML, so you could include the source code inside a </p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\"><pre><code>&lt;div style=\"hidden\"&gt;\n</code></pre>\n</div><p>block or similiar. Maybe give it an id that allows us to recognise it as containing diagram source.</p>\n<p>Definitely I’d suggest not to use the SVG editor. Actually I would like to remove it from the nLab, just haven’t got around to suggesting it yet.</p>","timestamp":1531293993,"subject":"Images instead of codes rendering","stream_id":1,"display_recipient":"nLab","reactions":[]},{"id":69001,"sender_id":11,"sender_full_name":"Urs","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b00d1ee17463af676c78974439b92471?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/1-nLab/topic/Images.20instead.20of.20codes.20rendering/near/69001\">#10</a></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Definitely I’d suggest not to use the SVG editor. Actually I would like to remove it from the nLab, just haven’t got around to suggesting it yet.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>When you do find the time (thanks!) maybe also remove the button right above, saying “Make this page and S5 slide show”. The only effect this button has had in the past is that users accidently generated spurious edits, which we then had to undo.</p>","timestamp":1531294365,"subject":"Images instead of codes rendering","stream_id":1,"display_recipient":"nLab","reactions":[]},{"id":69005,"sender_id":639,"sender_full_name":"Praphulla Koushik","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/4d3ba0c0a767b7329e0f56993aceb259?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/1-nLab/topic/Images.20instead.20of.20codes.20rendering/near/69005\">#11</a> Thanks @Richard williamson. I will try doing like that next time :)</p>","timestamp":1531301055,"subject":"Images instead of codes rendering","stream_id":1,"display_recipient":"nLab","reactions":[]},{"id":69006,"sender_id":11,"sender_full_name":"Urs","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b00d1ee17463af676c78974439b92471?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/1-nLab/topic/Images.20instead.20of.20codes.20rendering/near/69006\">#12</a> Praphulla Koushik, which diagrams specifically do you want to typeset?</p>","timestamp":1531304156,"subject":"Images instead of codes rendering","stream_id":1,"display_recipient":"nLab","reactions":[]},{"id":69008,"sender_id":639,"sender_full_name":"Praphulla Koushik","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/4d3ba0c0a767b7329e0f56993aceb259?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/1-nLab/topic/Images.20instead.20of.20codes.20rendering/near/69008\">#13</a> @Urs : Hello Sir,</p>\n<p>Most of the commutative diagrams, for example the diagram in  https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/cokernel</p>","timestamp":1531305166,"subject":"Images instead of codes rendering","stream_id":1,"display_recipient":"nLab","reactions":[]},{"id":69010,"sender_id":11,"sender_full_name":"Urs","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b00d1ee17463af676c78974439b92471?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/1-nLab/topic/Images.20instead.20of.20codes.20rendering/near/69010\">#14</a> For such simple diagrams, the available array-hacks seem to be sufficient:</p>\n<p><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><semantics><mtable rowspacing=\"0.16em\" columnalign=\"center center center\" columnspacing=\"1em\"><mtr><mtd><mstyle scriptlevel=\"0\" displaystyle=\"false\"><mi>A</mi></mstyle></mtd><mtd><mstyle scriptlevel=\"0\" displaystyle=\"false\"><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\"><mover><mo><mo>⟶</mo></mo><mi>f</mi></mover></mo></mstyle></mtd><mtd><mstyle scriptlevel=\"0\" displaystyle=\"false\"><mi>B</mi></mstyle></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mstyle scriptlevel=\"0\" displaystyle=\"false\"><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"true\" minsize=\"1.2em\" maxsize=\"1.2em\" lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">↓</mo></mstyle></mtd><mtd><mstyle scriptlevel=\"0\" displaystyle=\"false\"><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></msup></mstyle></mtd><mtd><mstyle scriptlevel=\"0\" displaystyle=\"false\"><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"true\" minsize=\"1.2em\" maxsize=\"1.2em\" lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">↓</mo></mstyle></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mstyle scriptlevel=\"0\" displaystyle=\"false\"><mn>1</mn></mstyle></mtd><mtd><mstyle scriptlevel=\"0\" displaystyle=\"false\"><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">⟶</mo></mstyle></mtd><mtd><mstyle scriptlevel=\"0\" displaystyle=\"false\"><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mstyle></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\n  \\begin{matrix}\n    A &amp;\\stackrel{f}{\\longrightarrow}&amp; B\n    \\\\\n    \\big\\downarrow &amp;{}^{(\\mathrm{po})}&amp; \\big\\downarrow\n    \\\\\n    1 \n      &amp;\\longrightarrow&amp; \n    \\mathrm{coker}(f)\n  \\end{matrix}\n</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:4.1522em;vertical-align:-1.8261em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mtable\"><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:2.3261em;\"><span style=\"top:-4.3261em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.3442em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.0781em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.3442em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"delimsizing mult\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.851em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.251em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.601em;\"></span><span class=\"delimsizinginner delim-size1\"><span>↓</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-2.843em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.601em;\"></span><span style=\"height:0.016em;width:0.6667em;\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"0.6667em\" height=\"0.016em\" style=\"width:0.6667em\" viewBox=\"0 0 666.67 16\" preserveAspectRatio=\"xMinYMin\"><path d=\"M312 0 H355 V16 H312z M312 0 H355 V16 H312z\"/></svg></span></span><span style=\"top:-2.851em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.601em;\"></span><span class=\"delimsizinginner delim-size1\"><span>⏐</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.35em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-1.8781em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.3442em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">1</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.8261em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:2.3261em;\"><span style=\"top:-4.3261em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.3442em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mrel\"><span class=\"mop op-limits\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.3442em;\"><span style=\"top:-3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span><span class=\"mop\">⟶</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.7581em;margin-left:0em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.011em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.0781em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.3442em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"></span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.888em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mopen mtight\">(</span><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathrm mtight\">po</span></span><span class=\"mclose mtight\">)</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-1.8781em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.3442em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mrel\">⟶</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.8261em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:2.3261em;\"><span style=\"top:-4.3261em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.3442em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0502em;\">B</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.0781em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.3442em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"delimsizing mult\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.851em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.251em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.601em;\"></span><span class=\"delimsizinginner delim-size1\"><span>↓</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-2.843em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.601em;\"></span><span style=\"height:0.016em;width:0.6667em;\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"0.6667em\" height=\"0.016em\" style=\"width:0.6667em\" viewBox=\"0 0 666.67 16\" preserveAspectRatio=\"xMinYMin\"><path d=\"M312 0 H355 V16 H312z M312 0 H355 V16 H312z\"/></svg></span></span><span style=\"top:-2.851em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.601em;\"></span><span class=\"delimsizinginner delim-size1\"><span>⏐</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.35em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-1.8781em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.3442em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">coker</span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.8261em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p>\n<p>To make this come out decently, just be sure to stretch the arrows: </p>\n<p>For horizontal arrows use <code>\\longrightarrow</code> instead of <code>\\to</code> or <code>\\rightarrow</code> and similarly <code>\\longleftarrow</code> etc.</p>\n<p>For vertical arrows use <code>\\big\\downarrow</code> instead of just <code>\\downarrow</code>, etc.</p>\n<p>The above is typeset with</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\"><pre><code>  \\array{\n    A &amp;\\stackrel{f}{\\longrightarrow}&amp; B\n    \\\\\n    \\big\\downarrow &amp;{}^{(po)}&amp; \\big\\downarrow\n    \\\\\n    1 \n      &amp;\\longrightarrow&amp; \n    coker(f)\n  }\n</code></pre>\n</div><p>It’s not perfect, but also not too bad.</p>","timestamp":1531306317,"subject":"Images instead of codes rendering","stream_id":1,"display_recipient":"nLab","reactions":[]},{"id":69011,"sender_id":639,"sender_full_name":"Praphulla Koushik","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/4d3ba0c0a767b7329e0f56993aceb259?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/1-nLab/topic/Images.20instead.20of.20codes.20rendering/near/69011\">#15</a> @Urs :</p>\n<p>It looks definitely better. I will try to imitate this idea where I think a diagram  can be made better. </p>\n<p>Thanks.</p>","timestamp":1531308039,"subject":"Images instead of codes rendering","stream_id":1,"display_recipient":"nLab","reactions":[]},{"id":69012,"sender_id":11,"sender_full_name":"Urs","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b00d1ee17463af676c78974439b92471?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/1-nLab/topic/Images.20instead.20of.20codes.20rendering/near/69012\">#16</a> Okay, good. You can further stretch horizontal arrows by labeling them with sufficient whitespace, such as <code>\\overset{\\phantom{AAAAA}}{\\longrightarrow}</code></p>\n<p><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo><mover><mo><mo>⟶</mo></mo><mphantom><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mrow></mphantom></mover></mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\overset{\\phantom{\\mathrm{AAA}}}{\\longrightarrow}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.3003em;vertical-align:-0.011em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\"><span class=\"mop op-limits\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.2893em;\"><span style=\"top:-3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span><span class=\"mop\">⟶</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.711em;margin-left:0em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\" style=\"color:transparent;\"><span class=\"mord mathrm mtight\" style=\"color:transparent;\">AAA</span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.011em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p>\n<p><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo><mover><mo><mo>⟶</mo></mo><mphantom><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mrow></mphantom></mover></mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\overset{\\phantom{\\mathrm{AAAA}}}{\\longrightarrow}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.3003em;vertical-align:-0.011em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\"><span class=\"mop op-limits\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.2893em;\"><span style=\"top:-3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span><span class=\"mop\">⟶</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.711em;margin-left:0em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 siz